comment.narrative:
An index will be used to measure &quot;effectiveness&quot; and the indicator will be scored accordingly on a scale of 0-5: 1 - meeting occurs; 2 - a quorum representing 60 percent of the membership is in attendance; 3 - Agenda shared in advance; 4 - Minutes from the meeting are shared; 5 - decision points acted upon, as reflected in the next meetings&rsquo; minutes. A score of 4 and above will constitute an effective meeting.

All quarterly meetings for 2023 have taken place to date and all meetings have been effective, meaning that minutes from the meetings have been shared with the task team, and key issues have guided implementation.&nbsp;

The end target refers to four effective quarterly meetings a year. Yet, four meetings can only be achieved at the end of each calendar year; the fourth meeting is scheduled for December 2023. Thus, while three meetings has been held so far in 2023, this corresponds to all required meetings for 2023 to date. As such, this indicator is achieved.

&nbsp;
